From 5860930326c2abfdeee0d234287a58fddf2c0373 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Til Goldan <til@goldan.dev>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:22:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gestures: don't let a clickpad click cancel an established
 multi-finger gesture

tp_gesture_post_events() forces single-finger pointer-motion mode (and
cancels any active gesture) whenever the clickpad button is pressed
while thumb.state == THUMB_STATE_FINGER, on the assumption that this
means the button is being pressed by a real finger, not a thumb resting
on it, and so the user wants an ordinary 1fg click-drag.

But THUMB_STATE_FINGER is the *default* classification, not "confirmed
not a thumb": tp_thumb_update_multifinger() explicitly resets to it via
tp_thumb_lift() whenever several touches land together within
THUMB_TIMEOUT, which is exactly what happens at the start of a genuine
3 or 4-finger swipe or pinch (this is deliberate, so multi-finger taps/
clicks/gestures aren't mistaken for a resting thumb). As a result,
thumb.state stays THUMB_STATE_FINGER for the whole lifetime of a normal
multi-finger gesture, so any physical click while those fingers are
still down -- e.g. an accidental harder press mid-swipe -- gets
misread as "start a 1fg click-drag" and cancels the gesture outright
(for 3fg-drag this also immediately releases the emulated BTN_LEFT).

Only fall back to forcing 1fg mode while finger_count is still below
3, i.e. while we don't yet know if this is a single real finger (or a
thumb-held click) rather than an already-recognized multi-finger
gesture. Once a swipe/pinch/3fg-drag is established, a click no longer
reinterprets it.

Stacked on top of bazzite-til's 0001/0002 patches.
---
 src/evdev-mt-touchpad-gestures.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/evdev-mt-touchpad-gestures.c b/src/evdev-mt-touchpad-gestures.c
index 52c1053c..bc3f5c08 100644
--- a/src/evdev-mt-touchpad-gestures.c
+++ b/src/evdev-mt-touchpad-gestures.c
@@ -2082,9 +2082,19 @@ tp_gesture_post_events(struct tp_dispatch *tp, usec_t time, bool ignore_motion)
 	/* When tap-and-dragging, force 1fg mode. On clickpads, if the
 	 * physical button is down, don't allow gestures unless the button
 	 * is held down by a *thumb*, specifically.
+	 *
+	 * This only applies while we don't yet know whether we have one or
+	 * several fingers down: thumb detection resets to THUMB_STATE_FINGER
+	 * (its default, not "confirmed not a thumb") whenever several touches
+	 * land together, which is exactly what happens at the start of a
+	 * real 3/4-finger swipe or pinch. Once finger_count is already 3 or
+	 * more we know we're in an established multi-finger gesture, so a
+	 * click shouldn't reinterpret it as a 1fg click-drag and cancel it.
 	 */
-	if (tp_tap_dragging(tp) || (tp->buttons.is_clickpad && tp->buttons.state &&
-				    tp->thumb.state == THUMB_STATE_FINGER)) {
+	if (tp_tap_dragging(tp) ||
+	    (tp->buttons.is_clickpad && tp->buttons.state &&
+	     tp->thumb.state == THUMB_STATE_FINGER &&
+	     tp->gesture.finger_count < 3)) {
 		if (tp->gesture.state != GESTURE_STATE_POINTER_MOTION) {
 			tp_gesture_cancel(tp, time);
 			tp_gesture_handle_event(tp,
